        "id": 89481,
        "name": "pyrofrog",
        "username": "pyrofrog",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pyrofrog/{size}/1963_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-07T06:31:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But that really doesn't have anything to do with what I was proposing.&nbsp; Catwoman is a \"thief\" much more than she is \"seductive\" … I was just thinking in terms of Ermine being a \"cat burglar\" in the conventional sense of the term.</p>\n<div>\n</div></blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I understand it isn't the comparison you were making, but it still seemed like a fun place to share that information.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My idea was that each of the Vengeance villains would be playable solo as a difficulty-1 villain, but that there would be synergies in their decks which would make them essentially square in difficulty for every one of them you fought (which I didn't assume was necessarily slaved to the number of heroes).&nbsp; Two of them together would be a difficulty-2 challenge, three would be a \"low 3\" (a la the un-advanced Ennead), four would be a \"high 3\" like the Dreamer or Miss Information, and five would be a difficulty-4 challenge akin to The Chairman.</p>\n\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>An interesting idea, and a lot of this could be done by changing the starting villain info. I think that each villain in vengeance has a different inherent difficulty. So simply scaling the number of them to increase the challenge could be problematic, and one combination of three of them is a different challenge rating than another group of three. (Again, this may just be my experience, but that is all I have at this time.). <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
